<title>FRANCE: Alcatel sees no EPS, debt damage from Thomson-CSF.</title>
<headline>Alcatel sees no EPS, debt damage from Thomson-CSF.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alcatel Alsthom chairman Serge Tchuruk said on Tuesday his group's offer for the 58 percent French state stake in Thomson-CSF would not raise Alcatel's debts, nor weigh on Alcatel earnings per share.</p>
<p>&quot;I repeat to my shareholders that this operation will not increase group indebtedness nor weigh on earnings per share,&quot; Tchuruk told Reuters after a news conference.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
